    <paragraph>Subtract Integers in Applications</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, solve the following applications.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="195" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Temperature One morning, the temperature in Urbana, Illinois, was $$\text{28° Fahrenheit.}$$ By evening, the temperature had dropped $$\text{38° Fahrenheit.}$$ What was the temperature that evening?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>−10°</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="196" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Temperature On Thursday, the temperature in Spincich Lake, Michigan, was $$\text{22° Fahrenheit.}$$ By Friday, the temperature had dropped $$\text{35° Fahrenheit.}$$ What was the temperature on Friday?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="197" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Temperature On January 15, the high temperature in Anaheim, California, was $$\text{84° Fahrenheit.}$$ That same day, the high temperature in Embarrass, Minnesota was $$\text{−12° Fahrenheit.}$$ What was the difference between the temperature in Anaheim and the temperature in Embarrass?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>96°</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="198" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Temperature On January 21, the high temperature in Palm Springs, California, was $$\text{89°,}$$ and the high temperature in Whitefield, New Hampshire was $$\text{−31°} .$$ What was the difference between the temperature in Palm Springs and the temperature in Whitefield?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="199" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Football At the first down, the Warriors football team had the ball on their $$\text{30-yard line.}$$ On the next three downs, they gained $$\text{2 yards,}$$ lost $$\text{7 yards,}$$ and lost $$\text{4 yards.}$$ What was the yard line at the end of the third down?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>21-yard line</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="200" has_solution="false">
